## 3. PROPOSED TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE

To deliver native mobile fluidity on iOS and Android while keeping backend infrastructure low-latency and cost-controlled:

* **Mobile Applications (Passenger & Driver):** Developed natively in **React Native** (TypeScript). This allows a single robust codebase to compile into native binary packages for **Apple iOS (App Store)** and **Google Android (Google Play Store)**, taking full advantage of native GPS sensors, hardware-accelerated map rendering, background push notifications, and biometric authentication.
* **Web Admin Dashboard:** Built using **Next.js (React)** styled with Tailwind CSS, delivering a responsive desktop and tablet control console for headquarters operations staff.
* **Backend API & Real-Time Engine:** **Node.js (NestJS)** utilizing high-throughput **WebSockets**. This handles sub-second driver coordinate broadcasting, ride dispatch matching, and immediate state synchronization across thousands of concurrent connections.
* **Database & Caching Tier:** **PostgreSQL** provides relational data storage for immutable financial ledgers, user credentials, and trip histories. **Redis** provides lightning-fast sub-second in-memory driver location caching and active booking sessions.
* **Cost-Controlled Geospatial Mapping:** Open-source tile rendering and routing engines (OpenStreetMap / Leaflet / Mapbox SDK bridges) combined with native mobile map rendering to prevent crippling third-party map API bills as trip volume scales.

